-- Surveyed cemetery lots, read from the traced plan vector: public/traces/
-- line detailed.svg. The grids there are boustrophedon serpentine paths rather
-- than one path per plot, so the polylines are walked, the two grid classes are
-- rasterised and each enclosed cell becomes a plot. Exact geometry, so the
-- count is whatever the trace says: 3890 interior plots.
-- Coordinates are the plan's own pixels on its 4096x3072 canvas.
--
-- Lot codes are S<plan section number>-<position in that section>, numbered
-- top-to-bottom then left-to-right. Price is the study's stated single-plot
-- value, carried here so a reservation's total is not zero.
--
-- Run after the schema is loaded: `make map-data`.
--
-- Re-running replaces the plots rather than adding to them, since the codes are
-- fixed and a duplicate would be rejected. Sections, users and accounts are left
-- alone; reservations and burials go with the plots they point at, because the
-- lots table is what they hang off.

DELETE FROM `cemetery_lots`;

